    LLM: 'Play hands with coordinated cardsâ€”same suits and close ranks for straights and flushes. Four random high cards are weaker than 9-10-J-Q double-suited.\n\nBlockers matter: if you hold two Aces, opponents are less likely to have nut flush draws. Fold marginal hands pre-flop; Omaha punishes loose play.\n\nEquity runs close; avoid overvaluing top set on a coordinated board. Nut draws (e.g. nut flush + straight draw) have strong implied odds.',
